Description:
 edulution-fileproxy - WebDAV server with SMB backend and NTLM authentication
Changes:
 edulution-fileproxy (1.6.2) noble; urgency=medium
 .
   * A file server that accepts the connection and then does not answer no
     longer hangs the service: every SMB login is bounded to 15 seconds and
     every logoff to 5 seconds, except in the startup signing probe, which
     bounds its login and logoff together to 15 seconds. Before, it blocked
     each WebDAV request that needed a new session, and
     edulution-fileproxy -t -user without limit.
   * edulution-fileproxy -t -user reports a file server that does not accept
     the connection and one that does not complete the login as separate
     timeouts.
   * A reindex that cannot connect to the file server, or whose SMB login
     times out, stops and keeps the previous index. Before, a login that did
     not answer hung it, and a refused connection replaced the index with
     one that missed the rest of the share.
   * The startup signing probe logs a file server that does not answer as
     unreachable, not as unable to sign.
   * An IPv6 address in smb.server works with and without brackets.
